// Binding a REFERENCE into a `let` local is routed for one narrow shape only:
// a `&mut` of a self-rooted place named directly. Every other reference
// binding measured has no route. Reduced from
// `samples/cli/systems/descriptor_walk`.
//
// Measured in a two-state machine (entry + a `done` state reached by a
// transition), each row differing from its neighbour by one token:
//
//   let d: &mut u32      = &mut main.size;          checks
//   let d: &mut u32      = &mut main.inner.a;       checks   (nested field)
//   let d: &mut [u8; 48] = &mut main.buf;           checks   (whole array)
//   let d: &mut u8       = &mut main.buf[0];        checks   (literal index)
//   let d: u32           = main.size;               checks   (a copy)
//
//   let d: &u32          = &main.size;              OMITTED
//   let d: &u32          = &main.inner.a;           OMITTED
//   let d: &[u8; 48]     = &main.buf;               OMITTED
//   let d: &u8           = &main.buf[0];            OMITTED
//   let d: &mut u8       = &mut main.buf[off];      OMITTED  (RUNTIME index)
//   let d: &mut Desc     = &mut main.buf[0] as &mut Desc;    OMITTED (recast)
//   let d: &mut u32      = &mut main.buf[0] as &mut u32;     OMITTED (recast
//                                                            to a non-record)
//   let v: u32 = 7; let d: &mut u32 = &mut v;       OMITTED  (borrow a LOCAL)
//   let v: u32 = 7; let d: &u32     = &v;           OMITTED, at a DIFFERENT
//                                                   phase, `state graph:
//                                                   result custody accounting`
//
// So: the SHARED `&` side has no route at all, at any depth and through any
// place. The `&mut` side routes only for a place that is self-rooted, indexed
// by a literal if indexed, and not recast.
//
// THE SAMPLE IS OVER-DETERMINED. `descriptor_walk`'s one line,
// `let d: &Desc = &main.buf[off] as &Desc;`, packs THREE independently
// sufficient triggers -- the shared borrow, the runtime index, and the recast
// -- each of which omits on its own against its own checking control. The
// board previously attributed the sample to the recast. That is not wrong, but
// it is incomplete in the way that matters: removing the recast alone leaves
// the sample omitting at the same site, so a repair aimed at any one trigger
// will not clear it. Confirm all three.
//
// This fixture pins the SHARED-BORROW trigger, the simplest of the three: no
// array, no record, no recast, no `requires`, no runtime index.
//
// A RECORD LITERAL carrying a reference field is one more producer, found
// while recovering a deleted termination customer:
// `Indirect { target: &mut owner }`, where `owner` is a plain local, omits at
// `statement sequence: local data: structural call binding` -- while the
// record literal alone checks and the bare `&mut owner` binding omits at
// `statement sequence: unsupported statement kind`. Pinned at
// `tests/omega/pending/termination/rank_endpoint_borrows_recovery`, which
// TERMINATION-RANKING-CHECKS is waiting on: that item asks to recover
// `rank_endpoint_borrows` as a corpus entry, and this is what stops it.
//
// The `&` of a plain local is listed above for completeness but is a
// DIFFERENT omission -- it reports `state graph: result custody accounting`,
// and it is reported to check when no transition follows, which was not
// re-measured here.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    size: u32;
}

machine Main::main(main: &mut Main) reaches Console {
    let borrowed: &u32 = &main.size;
    transition { _ -> done(main) }

    state done(main: &mut Main) {
        main.console.exit_process(0);
    }
}
